WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.140
Stranger Things is bonafide phenomenon, and
its charming young cast became stars, seemingly

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:05.640
overnight.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.160
Even though their careers are even younger
than they are, there are still some fascinating

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.760
factoids about each of the Netflix hit's kids.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:18.340
Like his onscreen alter ego Dustin Henderson,
Gaten Matarazzo really does live with a rare

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.480
bone disorder called cleidocranial dysplasia.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:25.470
While he’s said he has a relatively mild
case, he’s never developed collarbones or

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:26.460
permanent teeth.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:31.019
Matt and Ross Duffer, co-creators of the hit
series, decided to write that detail into

00:00:31.019 --> 00:00:34.750
the show after meeting Matarazzo, and the
young actor credits them with giving him a

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.440
platform from which to raise awareness for
his condition.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:43.380
“I told you a million times my teeth are
coming in, it's called cleidocranial dysplasia!”

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.350
Before the Duffer Brothers cast Matarazzo,
though, he had a tough time getting considered

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.880
for Hollywood roles as a result of his condition.

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:54.550
He did previously have some luck on Broadway,
however, and he also had a bit role on TV's

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.580
The Blacklist in 2015.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.380
Still, Stranger Things was the first full
series to give him a shot at stardom.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.180
Some kids are just born to be a part of the
biz.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.320
Finn Wolfhard inherited the entertainment
bug from his father, an aspiring screenwriter.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:11.500
And while his dad helped him develop an early
interest in movies, he's now trying to use

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:14.220
his own newfound influence to give his old
man an "in."

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:19.130
Thanks to Finn’s role in Stranger Things
and the 2017 adaptation of Stephen King’s

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:23.330
It, he’s been able to use his increased
pop culture profile to make connections along

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:27.120
with his old man, which was one of the reasons
he got into acting in the first place.

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:31.680
Aside from the It sequel, Finn landed a role
in the adaptation of the bestselling novel

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:36.340
The Goldfinch and joined the voice cast of
2019's animated Addams Family movie.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.420
On the show, Eleven is a young woman of few
words, but in real life, Millie Bobby Brown

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:44.140
has no trouble expressing herself with her
voice.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:48.800
Before she was Eleven, the British actress
had plenty of videos on her Youtube channel,

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:51.399
singing covers of Amy Winehouse, Adele, and
more.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:55.940
It almost makes you hope that Stranger Things
Season 3 throws in a full-on musical episode.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:59.760
It's her impressive acting chops, though,
that have people excited about her breakthrough

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:03.080
performance as the telekinetic superheroine
of the series.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:07.380
After shearing off her locks to play Eleven,
she’s definitely a star on the rise.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.860
At 13, she’s already been nominated for
two Emmy Awards, and she’s got a starring

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.760
role in Godzilla: King of the Monsters.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:19.020
Caleb McLaughlin got his start playing Young
Simba in Broadway's run of The Lion King around

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:22.210
the same time Gaten Matarazzo was on stage
in Les Mis.

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:27.350
The pair knew each other before Stranger Things,
and McLaughlin, like Matarazzo, can act, sing,

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:30.140
and dance, and even studied at the Harlem
School of the Arts.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.680
"Look, if you want to waste your time looking
for a traitor go ahead.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.240
because I'm not spending my time on her anymore!

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.000
No Way!"

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:41.500
While Stranger Things brought him to a new
worldwide audience, he hasn’t forgotten

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:45.570
how he got his start, telling Entertainment
Weekly that he and Matarazzo were constantly

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:48.520
singing familiar show tunes during their downtime
on the shoot.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:53.240
Steve Harrington went from a bit of a jerk
to a fan-favorite character over Stranger

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:57.890
Things’ two seasons, and Joe Keery can thank
his real-life niceness for inspiring a complete

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:59.300
overhaul of his character.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:03.290
His most likeable moment might not have come
from the show, though, and instead resulted

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:08.160
from Steve's visual similarity to a character
in the NBC sitcom Parks and Recreation.

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:12.560
Given their shared flair for big hair and
similar facial features, Stranger Things viewers

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.690
couldn't help but sense a connection between
Keery and Parks and Rec's Jean-Ralphio, played

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:17.620
by Ben Schwartz.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:22.080
The two actors embraced the gag, and even
made a viral video confirming that Steve is

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.630
Jean-Ralphio's secret father.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:24.420
“you’re my father.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:25.960
you’re my father.”

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:26.460
"What'd you just say?"

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:27.120
“you’re my father”

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:28.240
"Guys?"

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:30.100
“son”

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:35.440
While he was a major part of the second season,
Will Byers spent most of the first part of

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.180
Stranger Things stuck in the Upside Down.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:42.540
“Hello?

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:43.500
Hello?”

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:51.060
If that left you feeling like you were missing
out on seeing Noah Schnapp be menaced by evil

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:52.310
forces, don’t worry.

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:53.530
He was featured in Panic!

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:58.280
At the Disco’s music video for “LA Devotee,”
which featured him tethered to a chair by

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.380
a Satanic cult.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.410
It probably goes without saying that this
video was conveniently released right on the

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:07.870
heels of Stranger Things, and is probably
just the first in a long line of projects

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.980
following in the wake of his breakout performance.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:14.240
Natalia Dyer literally fell into acting when
she was a child.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:18.440
After spraining her ankle on the first day
of sports camp, her parents decided to put

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:22.540
her into a less physical program, and she
wound up studying drama instead.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:26.620
As a result, when she landed the role of the
lovable Nancy Wheeler, she’d already been

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:31.470
in the business for quite a few years, making
her on-screen debut way back in 2009 with

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:32.760
Hannah Montana: The Movie.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:37.220
She’s also been studying language at NYU,
but had to put her studies on hold due to

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:41.300
conflicts with filming her hit show, which
is a pretty good problem for a student to

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:41.800
have.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:47.500
Before her ill-fated character Barb inspired
some of 2016's most memorable memes, Shannon

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.420
Purser was working at a movie theater.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:53.760
Once the internet blew up with its demands
for "Justice for Barb," though, Purser decided

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:58.010
to quit her day job and give the biz a real
shot… and the Barb frenzy was responsible

00:04:58.010 --> 00:04:59.630
for that in more ways than one.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:00.880
“Are you sick of that yet?”

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:05.060
"A little bit, my mom called me Barb once
and uh that's when I knew it had gone a little

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:05.560
too far."

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:09.600
She told Glamour she actually had to let go
of her gig at the theater once her newfound

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:11.560
fanbase started showing up at her job.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:16.430
However it happened, Stranger Things launched
Purser into plenty of roles, including a recurring

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:21.980
part as Ethel Muggs in Riverdale and the lead
role in the 2018 Netflix film Sierra Burgess

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:22.960
Is a Loser.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:27.620
If you thought Jonathan Byers seemed to have
a lyrical soul, you know, whenever he wasn't

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:32.420
taking creepy pictures of Nancy, it's because
in addition to acting, he's also a musician.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:38.320
He played drums for Brit noise band Comanechi
until 2014, when they concluded an 18-month

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:39.870
world tour and called it quits.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:44.700
It was his sister who first prompted him to
pursue acting, and his first gig was an eight-minute

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:48.690
advertisement for a Swiss insurance company
complete with a full storyline.

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:53.500
Heaton wasn't so lucky in October of 2017,
when he missed the Season 2 premiere party

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:56.460
after being detained at Los Angeles International
Airport.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:01.260
Security examined his belongings and detected
a "very small amount" of a substance later

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.620
determined to be cocaine.

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:07.120
Heaton ended up being sent back to the U.K.,
a gaffe for which he apologized in a public

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:08.120
statement days later.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:13.820
Joining our Hawkins heroes in the second season
is another young lady with a supreme set of

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:16.340
skills, although hers have nothing to do with
telekinesis.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:21.080
Max, a transplant from California, owns the
high score on Dig Dug at the local arcade

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:25.270
under her pseudonym "Mad Max," and even though
some members of the group are a little more

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:29.720
reluctant than others to include her, she
eventually joins up with her prodigious skateboard

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:30.220
skills.

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:32.600
“And plus, she skateboards so she's pretty
awesome”

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:33.120
"Awesome?

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:35.020
You haven't even spoken a word to her!"

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:39.750
The actress behind all that sass, Sadie Sink,
grew close to Millie Bobby Brown on the set

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:44.060
of Stranger Things 2, despite the fact that
their characters share very little screen

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:44.560
time.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:49.680
The two enjoyed slumber parties together,
dueted on pop music covers, and spent downtime

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:50.740
from the shoot together.

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:55.140
But despite how close the pair grew behind
the scenes, Sink reportedly took a lot of

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:59.400
social media heat from fans who were afraid
Max might drive a wedge between Eleven and

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:03.480
Mike, which might have helped prepare her
for the controversy that erupted after she

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:07.650
revealed that her kiss with Caleb McLaughlin
toward the end of the second season was an

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:08.760
unscripted surprise.

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:13.560
There's a reason Priah Ferguson was promoted
to a recurring character between Stranger

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:18.720
Things' second and third seasons: her portrayal
of Lucas Sinclair's sassy little sister made

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:23.260
her an instant favorite during her brief time
in the series' sophomore run, as fans delighted

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:26.200
in her unbridled passion for syrup and sharp
demeanor.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:29.380
Behind the scenes, Ferguson is just as intriguing.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:33.820
Although her young career started to flourish
once she landed her role in the Netflix sci-fi

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:37.160
series her backup career plan is also pretty
impressive.

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:40.600
If acting doesn’t work out, she has plans
on becoming a surgeon.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:44.940
Ferguson's other ambition is to be a philanthropist,
and she's already well on her way.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:50.280
In 2015, the Georgia native landed a spokesmodeling
gig with United Way, and hopes to help the

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:50.780
homeless.

00:07:51.640 --> 00:07:56.200
Although she didn't start acting until her
late teens, Season 3 addition Maya Hawke has

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.740
been a part of Hollywood since the day she
was born.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:02.200
Hawke is the eldest child of actors Ethan
Hawke and Uma Thurman.

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:06.160
After spending her childhood visiting the
sets where her parents worked, she said she

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:08.340
finds acting to be as natural as breathing.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:13.020
Hawke, who struggled in school early on thanks
to her diagnosed dyslexia, earned a breakthrough

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:18.210
role as Jo March in the PBS adaptation of
Louisa May Alcott's Little Women, a role that

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:22.600
was so important to her that Hawke was willing
to quit her studies at Juilliard to take it.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:27.740
Before becoming the well-liked lifeguard Heather
in Hawkins, Indiana, Francesca Reale starred

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:30.690
in another big Netflix series: Haters Back
Off!

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:35.070
To get that role and her part in Stranger
Things, though, the NYU grad had to first

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:37.540
qualify for her Screen Actors Guild card.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:41.820
That meant having to start small, including
a bit part on Blue Bloods where she “laid

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:43.480
in a pile of dirt” as a dead body.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:45.700
That hasn’t stopped her from dreaming big.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:51.330
Citing Audrey Hepburn as her ultimate Hollywood
inspiration, she has aspirations to eventually

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:55.680
take her television successes to the silver
screen, and she's already well on her way.

00:08:55.960 --> 00:09:01.050
For her feature film debut, she was cast alongside
Stranger Things castmate Natalia Dyer in Karen

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:04.660
Maine's full-length adaptation of her short
film Yes, God, Yes.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:10.440
Last but not least, we have Billy, your prototypical
mean teen with a mullet, no shirt, and zero

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.420
respect for speed limits.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:16.200
He looks like a cross between Rob Lowe in
St. Elmo's Fire and Jason Patric in The Lost

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:18.820
Boys, but with fewer redeemable inner qualities.

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:24.000
In real life, Dacre Montgomery is hardly the
depraved character he portrays on the show.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:28.510
The Australia native spends his downtime making
music videos, and before Stranger Things,

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:33.500
he starred as Jason Scott, the Red Ranger
in 2017's big-screen Power Rangers movie.

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:38.380
In that film, he’s as easy to like as Billy
is to hate, which shows some pretty impressive

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:42.900
range, and probably came as a surprise to
plenty of Mighty Morphin fans who followed

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:43.700
him to Hawkins.

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:49.100
His initial audition for Stranger Things consisted
of one very thematically on-point mini-film

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:53.281
he made for the Duffer Brothers, in which
he, quote, “may or may not have put on a

00:09:53.281 --> 00:09:55.480
g-string and danced to 'Hungry Like a Wolf.'"

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:59.330
Nabbing the role was what made him decide
to move to the U.S. to pursue his budding

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:00.740
screen career once and for all.

